  "note": "First election for the restored council, which had been dissolved on 6 March 1934 and run by a commissioner (Belfast News-Letter, 7 March 1934). The boundary had been extended and the city divided into five wards of four seats. Results were declared early on 19 September; about 55 per cent of the electorate voted. No contest in this ward; the Unionist candidates were returned automatically.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Belfast News-Letter, 19 September 1946, p. 5 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the Frontier Sentinel prints 'G. Leburn' (kept in Name_As_Printed); the News-Letter prints 'George Leyburn', the form of his other returns, so he is recorded as G. Leyburn and the News-Letter report was added to the citation."
